[2026-05-08T19:53:05.225Z] [STDOUT] ## What
- Adds a `/translate` library, CLI, HTTP, and web surface that formalizes text first, then translates resolved Wikidata Q/P phrases through target-language labels.
- Extends `/formalize` with a CST rich enough to regenerate Markdown through `markdownFromFormalizationCst()`.
- Preserves unresolved source terms as variables with generated questions, and exposes translation Markdown, HTML, Links Notation, and CST output.
- Adds issue #16 case-study requirements, research notes, solution plan, captured GitHub/search data, and a web screenshot.

Fixes #16.

## Screenshot
![Translate page](https://github.com/link-assistant/meta-expression/blob/issue-16-a4cb3c8415b5/docs/case-studies/issue-16/translate-page.png?raw=true)

## Reproduction
- Before this change, `/formalize` results did not expose a reusable CST and there was no `/translate` API, CLI command, or web page that could translate formalized phrases.
- `tests/issue-16.test.js` reproduces that missing behavior by asserting the formalization CST, Markdown regeneration, translation of `Hawaii` to Russian `Гавайи`, unresolved-variable questions, CLI parsing, async CLI output, HTTP `/translate`, and the static web translate page wiring.

## Testing
- `node --test tests/issue-16.test.js`
- `deno test --allow-read tests/issue-16.test.js`
- `deno test --allow-read`
- `npm test`
- `npm run check`
- `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`
- `git diff --check`
- `GITHUB_BASE_REF=main node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs`
- Playwright smoke: `http://127.0.0.1:4173/web/#/translate`, `Hawaii` -> `Гавайи`
